; Co-hosted keys-list DEP spec (`--wrapper-requests` host side). The dep OWNS `stake_cred` (a real
; record) but its own spec produces NEITHER of the two requested shapes below. A consumer that
; borrows `{* stake_cred => uint}` also borrows `[* stake_cred]` for that map's `keys()` accessor, so
; both wrappers are co-hosted into THIS crate's `requested_collections.rs` in one run. The keys-list
; wrapper (`StakeCredList`) is minted in that same file, so the requested-collections import walk must
; NOT emit `use crate::generated::StakeCredList;` for it (the generated root defines no such name —
; E0432). Contrast the map's ELEMENT class `StakeCred`, which genuinely lives at the root and IS
; imported. `container` merely keeps `stake_cred` referenced as a struct.
stake_cred = [x: uint]
container = [c: stake_cred]
